=== PARITY (vs web FleetTelemetryHealth.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (FleetHealthSource -> FleetHealthModel):
    useTranslation, useFleetTelemetryErrorVINs, useFleetTelemetryErrors (+ the two Tesla-refresh
    mutations useRefreshFleetTelemetryError{VINs,s}). The production app wires FleetHealthSource by
    composing the error-VINs query with the VIN-filtered error-log query; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> FleetHealthProjection is a 1:1 port: isRecent(d) = now - d < 24h (nil never recent,
    future treated recent, matching the web signed comparison); empty code/message folds to the
    em-dash (web `?? '—'` / falsy `''`); vinBadgeTone = count>0 ? danger : success
    (web `vinList.length > 0`). Last-seen emphasis recent->rose / else->amber (web rose/amber);
    reported-at recent->rose / else->secondary (web rose/secondary). All verified by EXECUTED XCTest.
  Composition -> two ToolCard sections: "Error VINs" (exclamationmark.triangle.fill, danger) with the
    {n} affected badge + optional "Filtered: {vin}" badge (× clears) + "Refresh from Tesla"; and
    "Error Log" (exclamationmark.circle.fill, warning) with "Refresh from Tesla". VIN tap toggles the
    error-log filter (web setSelectedVin(r.vin === selectedVin ? '' : r.vin)).
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone / TSIconBox compiled
    against the REAL design tokens + real Badges.swift in the typechecks below. Recharts -> none /
    Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton rows) · empty ("No vehicles with telemetry errors" /
    "No fleet telemetry errors recorded") · error (QueryError-equivalent retry, native chrome since
    the web relies on react-query's implicit handling) · stale (chip + banner + one guarded auto-
    refresh) · offline (cached rows + chip + banner) · content; per section. Cached rows stay visible
    behind refresh/failure, matching the web shell.
  i18n -> all source strings resolve through the P1/S10 facade (table "FleetTelemetryHealth") with the
    web English fallback — the canonical devtools.health.* namespace (already in the shared catalog):
      errorVinsTitle, errorVinsDesc, affectedVehicles, filteredBy, clearVinFilter, refreshVins, vin,
      firstSeen, lastSeen, noErrorVins, errorLogTitle, errorLogDesc, refreshErrors, errorCode, message,
      reportedAt, noErrors  + native chrome (live/stale/offline/staleBanner/offlineBanner/loading/
      errorTitle/retry/filterHint) — ALL present in FleetTelemetryHealth.strings. No English literal
      in Swift.
  a11y -> each VIN row is one labeled, selectable button (full-row tap toggles the filter) carrying the
